BACKGROUND

Run Lisp in background, own REPL, own thread. Get job id at once; keep working.

  (setq j (background (fetch-report) :fork t :deadline 60))
  (background '(+ 1 2))                  ; fresh REPL by default
  (background (scan) :permissions "(permission/deny \"fs/*\")")
  (background-state j)                   ; :pending :held :done :failed :cancelled :lost
  (background-wait j)                    ; wait now, return printed value
  (background-cancel j)                  ; t if cancelled

:fork t = copy of your image now. :permissions only narrow your rules.
:deadline in seconds. Not waited? Value comes later as
<system-event source="background:<job>">, wakes you if turn ended. Asks from
job reach user in root chat. Job ids survive restart in your image.

Watch, all times in ms:

  (sleep 500)
  (poll-until (ready-p) :every 1000 :timeout 30000)
  (watch-until (status) (lambda (s) (equal s "up")) :every 2000 :timeout 60000)
  (retry 5 :backoff (backoff :exponential :base 100 :factor 2 :max 5000 :jitter 0.1) (call-api))
  (backoff :constant :base 1000)         ; also :linear, :factor = ms added each try
  (backoff-delay (backoff :exponential :base 100) 3) ; => 800
  (with-timeout 5000 (await p))
  (every 1000 :times 3 (check))          ; list of 3 values

Past :timeout, poll-until, watch-until, with-timeout raise error. retry raises
last error. every without :times runs until cancel or deadline: run it in
background.
